.TH DYMUS 1 "" "Dymus @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dymus \- keyboard-driven music player with terminal and headless interfaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dymus
.br
.B dymus search
.I query
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dymus play
.I target
.RI [ query ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dymus download
.I target query
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dymus local
.RI [ query ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B dymus control
.I action
.br
.B dymus auth
.I action
.br
.B dymus lastfm
.I action
.br
.B dymus doctor
.br
.B dymus man
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dymus plays YouTube Music, YouTube video, and local media using mpv.
With no command, it opens the keyboard-driven terminal interface (TUI).
Headless commands provide interactive selection, inline progress, detached
playback, downloads, and transport controls without opening the TUI.
.PP
Public search and local playback do not require a YouTube account.
Signed-in library access uses browser-session credentials configured with
.BR "dymus auth paste" or
.BR "dymus auth browser" .
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help for the selected command.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the application version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "search " query
Search all YouTube, select a result, and choose audio or video playback.
.B \-\-json
prints results without prompting or playing.
.BI "\-\-limit " number
sets the result count (1 to 50).
.B \-\-video
selects video without the mode prompt.
.B \-\-detach
returns to the shell while playback continues.
.BI "\-\-volume " number
sets initial volume (0 to 100; default 80).
.TP
.BI "play song|album|playlist " query
Find and play a song or a complete collection.
.TP
.BI "play library " category
Choose a signed-in library item.
Categories are
.BR playlists ,
.BR albums ,
.BR artists ,
and
.BR podcasts .
.TP
.BR "play local " [ query ]
Browse downloaded and imported local collections, or play a file, directory,
or UTF-8 M3U/M3U8 playlist.
.BI "\-\-path " path
reads a specific location.
.BI "\-\-id " id
selects an entire collection by the ID from
.BR "dymus local \-\-json" .
.B \-\-all
queues all tracks in matching collections without prompting.
.TP
.BI "download song|video|album|playlist " query_or_URL
Download audio or video using yt-dlp and ffmpeg.
The video target selects video automatically.
.B \-\-video
selects video for any target.
.BI "\-\-path " directory
overrides the configured destination.
Completed files, collection metadata, and relative M3U8 playlists are kept
if a download is interrupted; rerun the command to resume.
.TP
.BR "local " [ query ]
List local collections and tracks.
.B \-\-json
prints structured metadata and collection IDs.
.BI "\-\-path " path
reads a specific file, directory, or playlist.
.TP
.BI "control " action
Control the running headless player. Actions are
.BR status ,
.BR pause ,
.BR resume ,
.BR toggle ,
.BR next ,
.BR previous ,
.BR stop ,
and
.BI "volume " number
(0 to 100).
.TP
.BI "auth " action
.B paste
privately accepts and validates a YouTube Music Cookie header.
.B browser
imports YouTube Music cookies from a yt-dlp-supported browser, then validates the session.
.BI "\-\-browser " name
selects brave, chrome, chromium, edge, firefox, opera, safari, vivaldi, or whale
(default firefox; availability depends on the installed yt-dlp version).
.BI "\-\-profile " profile
selects a browser profile name or path; by default yt-dlp chooses the active profile.
.BI "\-\-container " name
selects a Firefox Multi-Account Container (Firefox only).
.BI "\-\-keyring " name
selects the Chromium cookie keyring on Linux: basictext, gnomekeyring, kwallet,
kwallet5, or kwallet6.
.BI "\-\-auth-user " index
selects the account index (default 0).
.B status
validates the saved session;
.B logout
removes it.
.TP
.BI "lastfm " action
.B login
authorizes a Last.fm session through a browser;
.B paste
privately accepts existing API and session credentials;
.B status
checks the connection;
.B logout
removes Last.fm credentials.
.TP
.B doctor
Check playback, download, and optional visualizer dependencies.
.TP
.B man
Write this manual in roff format to standard output.
.B \-\-install
installs it to the user's man directory.
.BI "\-\-directory " directory
selects a different man root, with the page stored under
.BR man1/dymus.1 .
This option requires
.BR \-\-install .
.SH PLAYBACK OPTIONS
All
.B play
targets accept:
.TP
.B \-\-video
Play video for each track. Streaming height is capped by
.B video_height
(default 1080 pixels); local files play at their original resolution.
.TP
.B \-\-detach
Keep playback running after the command exits.
.TP
.BI "\-\-volume " number
Set initial volume from 0 to 100 (default 80).
.PP
Headless selection accepts a result number followed by Enter.
Use n/p followed by Enter to change pages, and q, Esc, or Ctrl+C to cancel.
Ctrl+C cancels loading, stops attached playback, or cancels downloading.
Detached playback remains available through
.B dymus control
and MPRIS.
.SH TUI KEYS
These are the default bindings; many can be changed under
.B [keybindings]
in the configuration file.
.TP
.B /, Enter
Search, or filter the local library; play the selected track.
.TP
.B j/k, Up/Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B h, e, 1\-4, o, 5
Home, Explore, library categories, World Radio, and local library.
.TP
.B L
Refresh the local library.
.TP
.B Tab, t
Switch views; open Now Playing.
.TP
.B Space, n, r
Pause/resume, next track, retry playback.
.TP
.B V
Toggle a compact video window and audio-only playback.
The current position and pause state are preserved across a brief reload.
.TP
.B P, Q, a, A
Play all, queue all, queue a selection, play a selection next.
.TP
.B x, v, d, J/K
Mark, select all, remove, and reorder queue entries.
.TP
.B Left/Right, \-/+
Seek five seconds; change volume.
.TP
.B ?, s, q, Ctrl+C
Help, settings, quit, quit from any mode.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The TOML configuration is stored at
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dymus/config.toml ,
or
.I ~/.config/dymus/config.toml
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or empty.
Missing settings use built-in defaults.
.PP
.B video_height
sets the streaming video cap (default 1080; range 144 to 4320).
.B headless_search_results
sets full YouTube search results (default 10; range 1 to 50).
.B headless_results
sets YouTube Music collection search results (default 5; range 1 to 25).
.B start_view
can be set to "local" to open directly into the offline library.
.PP
.B [local]
accepts additional
.B roots
(default []),
.BR include_downloads ,
.BR scan_unindexed ,
.BR recursive ,
.BR read_tags ,
and
.BR video .
All five switches default to true.
ffprobe reads and caches local tags when available; filenames provide fallback metadata.
.PP
.B [downloads]
sets
.B audio_path
(default "~/Music/Dymus"),
.B video_path
(default "~/Videos/Dymus"),
.B audio_format
(default "mp3"),
.B video_format
(default "mp4"),
optional
.BR video_height ,
quality, naming, metadata, playlist, resume, archive, and progress settings.
By default, downloads are organized under Singles, Albums, and Playlists,
with numbered collection tracks, library.json, artwork, and relative M3U8 playlists.
.PP
.B lastfm_scrobbling
and
.B report_history
control optional Last.fm and YouTube Music reporting.
Local tracks can scrobble to Last.fm but never submit YouTube history.
See the project README for all configuration settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dymus/config.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/dymus/auth.json
YouTube Music session credentials.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dymus/
Headless control socket, state, and integration log.
The configuration directory is used when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unavailable.
.TP
.I library.json
Portable local-library index in a download destination.
.TP
.I .dymus/playlists/*.m3u8
Portable ordered playlists in a download destination.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1/dymus.1
User-installed manual. The default data directory is
.IR ~/.local/share .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the configuration directory.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Override the base for headless runtime files.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Override the data directory used by
.BR "dymus man \-\-install" .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color in headless feedback.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
mpv is required for playback. yt-dlp is required for streaming and downloads.
ffmpeg and ffprobe are required for downloads; ffprobe is optional for
imported local metadata. PipeWire's pw-dump and pw-record enable optional
reactive visualizers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dymus
dymus search "Nujabes Feather"
dymus search "live jazz" \-\-json \-\-limit 20
dymus play album "Modal Soul" \-\-detach
dymus play song "Feather" \-\-video
dymus local \-\-json
dymus play local ~/Music/mix.m3u8 \-\-detach
dymus play local \-\-path /media/music \-\-all
dymus download playlist "Jazz" \-\-path ~/Music/Jazz
dymus control volume 65
dymus control stop
dymus man \-\-install
man dymus
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success or interactive cancellation.
Nonzero indicates a configuration, dependency, network, or playback error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR man (1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/britonmearsty/dymus
